{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "486539c7-8a7e-8846-83fc-55a5896224b7",
  "created_at": "2026-02-24T18:36:16-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Patrick Doyle",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:11-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Lorraine. City Hall's closed for the day, but I'm here on the line. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:19-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, um, I'm calling about a drain, the low spot at the end of my block. It's, uh, under about a foot of water right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:29-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A foot of water. Okay, and where is that? What street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ayrault Street. I'm at 87, and it's down at the end, where it dips, by the corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:40-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "87 Ayrault Street, and the flooding is at the low spot at the end of the block. Is that the storm drain that's backed up, or is it just pooling?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:34:51-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think the drain's blocked, nothing's going down. It's been like this since the nor'easter, last weekend, Saturday into Sunday. Two days now and it's still sitting there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:01-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, since the storm over the weekend. Is it getting into anybody's property, or is it mostly in the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:08-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just the road, for now. But traffic's slowing to a crawl going through it, people are creeping along, and somebody's gonna stall out. I'd have called earlier but, um, my manager asked me to cover a shift, so I'm kind of rushing here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:23-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood, I'll be quick. So I have a storm drain blocked at the low spot at the end of Ayrault Street near number 87, about a foot of standing water, traffic crawling through. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:36-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, that's it. Honestly it's the kind of thing that should've been cleared by now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:42-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. I'll put it in as a work order for a crew to look at the drain. Can I get a number to reach you at?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:52-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, it's 401-555-0187."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:54-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0187. And that's Mr. Doyle?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:35:57-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Patrick Doyle, yeah. Can somebody call me back when it's done? Just so I know it's cleared."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:36:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll note that on the order, a callback to you once the crew's finished. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:36:09-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Thanks. I gotta run."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:36:12-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Mr. Doyle. Good luck with the shift."
    }
  ],
